## Overview

Every API call counts against the SLO of its plan. When the error budget for the month is spent, deploys stop.
The API is linked once per section; later uses of API in the same section stay plain text.

Code (`API`), links ([API reference](https://example.com/api)), URLs (https://example.com/API) and
attribute values ([plan]{.API}) never become terms, and neither does API-first or API.md.

## Operations

On call, the error budget is the first thing to check. Burn rate is how fast it is spent.

### The API in this section

Headings keep their ids: the heading above is still `#the-api-in-this-section`, while the API in this
paragraph is linked again because a new section has started.

## Glossary

:::glossary Terms and abbreviations
- **API**: Application Programming Interface, the HTTP interface of the service.
- **SLO**: Service level objective: the target share of good requests, e.g. 99.9% over 30 days.
- **Error budget**: How much unreliability the SLO allows in a period, as a share of requests.
  Spending it pauses risky deploys.
- **Burn rate:** How fast the error budget is being spent; `1` spends it exactly in the period.
:::
